    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the start, we receive a form."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicitly starts the process and describes the initial reception action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After receiving the form, we check if it is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the completeness verification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it needs to be sent back, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch splits the flow. Guard captures the condition. Splitting the textual termination into explicit send-back and end actions preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if we need to check the income, we continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard captures the continuation condition; action models the income check."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the same time, we complete the following steps: checking deductibles and checking the house."
      ],
      "justification": "Merges the two sub-steps into a single equivalent action. Behaviour is preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If we need to check the declaration, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Second decision point and its outcome branch. Correctly models the termination condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n11",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if we need to invite the declarant, the process also ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Alternative branch condition and subsequent actions. Faithfully restates the source logic."
    }
  ],
